https://click.email.judgejoeforcongress.com/?qs=cfc2a0ab508937daa6b0aa66e8f0a07e44409a5962caac4aaafcdf9ea80e3f07d6d7c83fcdad08f6679fd91f097bdf898669559f18293fb0e2979ca442252229
CHIP IN AND FIGHT BACK NOW

If U.S. manufacturers insist on gutting our workforce by outsourcing American jobs, then those companies should have to pay a price. Tariffs are a double-edged sword and currently out of fashion with the elites at cocktail parties in D.C., but, the men and women who clock out before having a beer after work, they know tariffs are a necessary tool to protect their livelihoods. The deck has been stacked against blue collar workers for far too long and it is time to consider using every weapon in our arsenal to finally do something about it.

Eric Sorensen is part of the problem.

While he regurgitates anti-Trump billionaire Mark Cuban&rsquo;s nonsense talking points,I&rsquo;ve been spending my time talking face-to-face with the folks right here in the district. They are being directly affected by outsourcing and are victims of this economic crisis created by the Administration&rsquo;s fiscal malpractice.

https://click.email.judgejoeforcongress.com/?qs=cfc2a0ab508937daa6b0aa66e8f0a07e44409a5962caac4aaafcdf9ea80e3f07d6d7c83fcdad08f6679fd91f097bdf898669559f18293fb0e2979ca442252229

Sorensen supports the very same policies &ndash; higher taxes, deficit spending, endless regulation &ndash; that are making it difficult to do business in the United States. Yet, when his policies harm the very workers he pretends to care about, he sides with the elites because he doesn&rsquo;t understand or care about economic reality for regular folks.

With Sorensen, the writing is on the wall. He&rsquo;ll continue to rubberstamp the same Biden-Harris policies that got us into this mess.

Not me!
